From e9daad686c4ab6bf9c8225862b6fab1f4dc870a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:31:21 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 28/29] inkling2: faster prompt passes for Mini at depth: whole
 2,048-row calls and fp8 keys widened once a call

Mini's prompt chunks split into calls of 1,024 / 512 / 256 rows past 128K, 256K and 512K because the shared
partials held 8 global chunks a row; they now hold every chunk of the context (0.8 GB a rank at 1M), so each
2,048-row chunk is one call at any depth (Small unchanged). On fp8 caches each global visit's prompt call first
widens the slot's keys to bf16 in the bf16 prompt kernel's layout (tf_ink2_kv_widen, tf_ink2_attn_prompt8's
tile values), then runs tf_ink2_attn_prompt: the same tile values into the same mma sequence, at the bf16 kernel's
speed. tf-inkling2-engine ptiming times one chunk at given depths and hashes chunk logits for A/B checks.
